# The built-in interface, parsed like any addon's `.toc`. Entries load in order: a bare filename
# is ours, from `assets/ui`; a path is the reference's own file, off the player's patch chain.
# The list loads on entering the world, then third-party addons. Deviation: entry 0, Fonts.xml,
# loads alone at Startup, because the glue screens share its glyph atlas.
# A frame built at load resolves `inherits=`, `parent=` and a named `relativeTo=` against names
# declared above; a missing one only warns (the template is skipped, the parent falls back to the
# enclosing frame).
# On a collision a later Lua global or template replaces the earlier one, but a named frame
# publishes its global only while the name is free.
# A stock `.xml` that does not `<Script file=>` its own `.lua` needs both rows, `.lua` first
# (`every_chain_xml_brings_its_own_lua`).
# Blizzard's LoadOnDemand addons have no row, as in the reference: `ui_script::addons` loads each
# off the chain on first use, after every template here is registered.

## Interface: 11200
## Title: benilla

Interface\FrameXML\Fonts.xml

# Second, not first as in the reference, because entry 0 must be Fonts.xml. The VM already ran it
# at Startup; this pass makes the manifest complete, and stock files read the strings at load.
Interface\FrameXML\GlobalStrings.lua
# `Localize()` runs at load and overwrites GlobalStrings keys, so this follows them.
Interface\FrameXML\Localization.xml
# `GetText` and its gender and plural helpers: a Lua global, not an engine binding (the client's
# `FrameScript_GetText` at `0x703bf0` calls it). UIParent.xml sources this file again.
Interface\FrameXML\LocaleProperties.lua
Interface\FrameXML\BasicControls.xml
# Before UIParent.xml, whose `LowHealthFrame` has `parent="WorldFrame"`.
Interface\FrameXML\WorldFrame.xml
# Above every file that names `parent="UIParent"` or adds a `UIPanelWindows` row at load.
# `ui_script::manifest` reruns `UIParent_ManageFramePositions` once the whole list has loaded.
Interface\FrameXML\UIParent.xml
Interface\FrameXML\ItemButtonTemplate.xml
# Before GameTooltip.xml and StaticPopup.xml, whose money rows inherit `SmallMoneyFrameTemplate`.
Interface\FrameXML\MoneyFrame.lua
Interface\FrameXML\MoneyFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\MoneyInputFrame.lua
Interface\FrameXML\MoneyInputFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\GameTooltip.xml
Interface\FrameXML\UIDropDownMenu.xml
Interface\FrameXML\UIMenu.xml
# Before the unit frames: their dropdowns' OnLoad runs `UIDropDownMenu_Initialize`, whose
# initializer calls `UnitPopup_ShowMenu` at once.
Interface\FrameXML\UnitPopup.xml
Interface\FrameXML\ItemRef.xml
# The `TextStatusBar` template and verbs, which the unit bars and `MainMenuExpBar` inherit.
Interface\FrameXML\TextStatusBar.lua
Interface\FrameXML\TextStatusBar.xml
# Before PartyFrame.xml, whose rows reach `RefreshBuffs` from their OnLoad.
Interface\FrameXML\BuffFrame.xml
# Two function-only kits: the unit windows below call `UnitFrame_Initialize` from their OnLoad,
# and the player and pet frames `CombatFeedback_Initialize`.
Interface\FrameXML\UnitFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\CombatFeedback.xml
Interface\FrameXML\PlayerFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\PartyFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\TargetFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\PetFrame.xml
# Anchors `relativeTo="TargetFrame"`.
Interface\FrameXML\ComboFrame.xml
# Ours: benilla's scroll kits, for our options window and script log.
ScrollTemplates.xml

Interface\FrameXML\UIPanelTemplates.lua

Interface\FrameXML\UIPanelTemplates.xml
# The reference's three options windows, loaded hidden so addons find their frames by name;
# nothing of ours may show them. Deviation: the player opens benilla's own options window,
# `OptionsFrame.xml` below. The video window's templates (OptionsFrameTemplates.xml) inherit
# UIPanelTemplates.xml's, and its dropdowns run `UIDropDownMenu_Initialize` at load. It holds the
# global `OptionsFrame`, so ours is `BenillaOptionsFrame`.
Interface\FrameXML\OptionsFrame.xml
Interface\FrameXML\SoundOptionsFrame.xml
# Inherits `OptionsCheckButtonTemplate`; brings CharacterFrameTemplates.xml and declares
# `UIOptionsFrameCheckButtons`, which MultiActionBars.lua writes at load.
Interface\FrameXML\UIOptionsFrame.xml
# StaticPopup.lua starts `StaticPopupDialogs` empty: a file that adds a dialog at load follows it.
Interface\FrameXML\StaticPopup.xml
Interface\FrameXML\CoinPickupFrame.xml

# Ours: the options window's Keybindings page. Before OptionsFrame.xml, whose Keybindings page
# inherits these templates and calls this script at OnLoad.
KeyBindingsPage.xml

# Ours: `BenillaOptionsFrame`, the options window the game menu opens. Its rows read
# `OptionsFrameSliders` and the option globals the stock windows above set at load.
OptionsFrame.xml

# Declares `MainMenuBar`, `MainMenuBarArtFrame` and `MainMenuExpBar`, which later files use as a
